  "body": "What: Let the machine file define vacuum zones (rectangles on the table) and the code that turns each zone on and off. The nest places parts so that each part, mainly a small part, sits on an active zone. The post emits the zone codes at sheet start.\n\nWhy: Laguna says a nest that ignores vacuum zones makes parts lift during the cut. Thermwood passes zone codes as machine code. #2161 has a small-before-large order but no zone data.\n\nSources: https://info.lagunatools.com/optimize-cabinet-cnc-nesting-for-better-sheet-yield , https://www.thermwood.com/updates_control_nesting_home.htm\n\nPart of #2395. Needs design: zone model, which parts need a zone, how the nest uses it.\n\nDone means: a design comment, then a nest test where a part never leaves its active zone, and a golden G-code test for the zone codes.\n",
